% The Daml Script token_test_2 of the project Daml intro, Daml Script: tokens a party may only issue to itself, run on its twin (token.le, which this program extends).

the target language is: lps.

the knowledge base token_token_test_2 extends token.

the maximum time is 6.

the knowledge base token_token_test_2 includes:

% Daml (the script run on a Canton sandbox) ends with these active contracts (their payloads;
% the ids are the ledger's):
%   - token(alice)
%   - token(bob)
% The twin's final state under LPS2 (`lps state`) is compared with it by test_daml.pl.
scenario token_test_2 is:
    % the Daml Script token_test_2
    % Daml refuses the next command (submitMustFail): the twin's integrity constraints refuse it
    alice creates the token c1 with owner bob from 1 to 2.
    % Daml refuses the next command (submitMustFail): the twin's integrity constraints refuse it
    bob creates the token c2 with owner alice from 2 to 3.
    alice creates the token c3 with owner alice from 3 to 4.
    bob creates the token c4 with owner bob from 4 to 5.

